  "body": "Call for an exclusive private viewing! \r\nThe Vendor has cherished this home for 22 years and is now looking to sell - this is an opportunity not to be missed.\r\n\r\nOwn a piece of Devonport history. Originally built in the early 1900s, Elizabeth House is a beautifully preserved heritage building that once stood as a grand waterfront home and now holds just a small number of exclusive apartments. The quality construction and elegant character are reminiscent of a bygone era. Combined with the unbeatable position along the prestigious King Edward Parade waterfront, and its proximity to Devonport Village, this is a rare opportunity to own a piece of Devonport’s history.\r\n\r\nWith the waterfront on your doorstep, this apartment is the epitome of Devonport living. Enjoy the ever-changing harbour views from the comfort of your living room. The open plan living, kitchen and dining area flow effortlessly through elegant French doors to your large, sunny and exclusive courtyard – perfect for alfresco dining or outdoor entertaining.  This private oasis is your sanctuary. \r\n\r\nThis apartment features a flexible floorplan with two spacious bedrooms, plus also a third room which can be used as a study or guest bedroom. Great for those who work from home. Each bedroom with their own ensuite and built-in wardrobes. \r\n\r\nLocated just a short, flat walk from the Devonport Village – the lifestyle on offer here is unbeatable. Enjoy fabulous cafes and restaurants at your leisure. The ferry to the CBD is close-by for your short scenic commute. You are moments away from Torpedo Bay beach, so you can swim before breakfast. The hum of Devonport’s community is here for you to take advantage of – so don’t miss out on this seldom available waterfront opportunity. Luxurious, low-maintenance living starts here.",
